note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/bwhz.om: the scoreboard hazard checker of gpu/nvidia/om/codegen/bw_hazard.om and
note bw_hazard_dec.om against the C it succeeds, src/omega_bw_hazard.c at 60b5d81e (DRA-606: a scoreboard barrier
note field holding 6 is refused, either field; src_pc is the smallest producer pc, whatever the visit order).
note Composed after bw_hazard.om, bw_hazard_dec.om and gpu/nvidia/checks/lib.om; run with gpu/nvidia/checks/bwhz.tsv.
note Rows, lowercase hex:
note d WORDS RC WBAR RBAR WAIT: hz_dec of the 16 bytes WORDS refuses (-1) exactly when RC is 1, and otherwise
note gives the write barrier, read barrier and wait mask of the C decode (record words 4, 5, 6). The oracle writes
note 0 0 0 for a refused row, and a refused row passes only with those zeros, so every byte of every row is read
note (the gate's table control changes the last byte of the first row, a refused one).
note j DT SV ST TAG: hz_jtag, the join's pc tag. l R RT PC TAG: hz_ltag, a late reader's. w V T TAG: hz_wtag, the
note tag of an entry after a wait. TAG is the C's expression on its own pmin (bwhz_oracle.c, README.md Oracles).
note The whole check, hz_chk, takes a 3203584-word wire: more than a program may hold in local arrays, and a global
note is never an argument, so it is not run here; README.md (bwhz) says how it was compared with the C.
text t_name "BWHZ"
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
fn bzx i ulong to ulong
n = cklen i
if or eq n 0 gt n 16
ckbad
end
v = ulong 0
for j ulong n bound 16
v = or shl v 4 cknib ckch i j
end
ret v
end
fn crow to bool
if ne cklen 0 1
ckbad
end
k = ckch 0 0
if eq k 106
ret crowj
end
if eq k 108
ret crowl
end
if eq k 119
ret crowt
end
if ne k 100
ckbad
end
ret crowd
end
fn crowd to bool
if ne ckcnt 6
ckbad
end
if ne ckhexn 1 16
ckbad
end
b = new uchar 16 0
d = new ulong 24 0
for j ulong 16
put b j uchar ckhex 1 j
end
rc = hz_dec b d
rr = bzx 2
if gt rr 1
ckbad
end
if eq rr 1
ok = eq rc long -1
ok = and ok eq bzx 3 0
ok = and ok eq bzx 4 0
ret and ok eq bzx 5 0
end
if ne rc 0
ret false
end
ok = eq get d 4 bzx 3
ok = and ok eq get d 5 bzx 4
ret and ok eq get d 6 bzx 5
end
fn crowj to bool
if ne ckcnt 5
ckbad
end
t = hz_jtag bzx 1 bzx 2 bzx 3
ret eq t bzx 4
end
fn crowl to bool
if ne ckcnt 5
ckbad
end
t = hz_ltag bzx 1 bzx 2 bzx 3
ret eq t bzx 4
end
fn crowt to bool
if ne ckcnt 4
ckbad
end
t = hz_wtag bzx 1 bzx 2
ret eq t bzx 3
end
